    "caption": "So says potato geneticist Ingo Hein. It’s due to the chaos which results when two potato plants are crossed. The result can be one of tens of thousands of variations, which is challenging when you just want to combine a few favourable traits. As Professor Hein explains, potato geneticists are using all the tools in the box to painstakingly come up with new potato varieties to suit the demands of modern agrifood in a changing climate.\n\nThe humble spud — Is the potato a hero or a dud? – Every Bite, ABC Radio National, October 17, 2026\n\nGuest\nIngo Hein\nHead of Potato Genetics\nDeputy Director\nNational Potato Innovation Centre\nJames Hutton Institute\n\nProfessor of Crop Genetics\nUniversity of Dundee\nAberdeen Scotland\n\nPresenter\nBelinda Smith",
